== Condensed Matter I — Mid term proposal and Final presentation guide

==== 1. Overview <id-1-overview>

The midterm assessment for Condensed Matter I is a *written proposal for your final presentation project*.

The proposal accounts for *25% of your total semester grade* and is due during:

#quote(block: true)[*October 27–30*]The purpose of the proposal is to make sure that, well before the final examination, you have identified a meaningful condensed matter physics question and developed a concrete plan for understanding it.

This is *not* simply a topic-selection form.

For example,

#quote(block: true)["I want to give my final presentation on topological insulators."]is a topic choice, but it is not yet a proposal.

A successful proposal should make clear:

#quote(block: true)[*What physical question will I investigate? Why is it nontrivial? What is the simplest model or theoretical framework that captures the physics? What calculation or argument will I use? What do I expect to learn?*]The proposal represents the first stage of your final project:

$ boxed "topic"arrow.r "question"arrow.r "minimal model"arrow.r "method"arrow.r "expected physics" $
You are *not expected to have completed the final project* by the proposal deadline. However, you should have done enough preliminary work to demonstrate that you understand the problem and have a realistic path toward the final presentation.

#line(length: 100%, stroke: gray)

